  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Song for Layne Staley**: rare: 6 archived performances [3]\n- **Crying on Eddie Nash's Grave**: rare: 6 archived performances [3]\n- **Charlie Sheen Reaches Out to the Feds**: rare: 14 archived performances [3]\n- **Letter From a Motel**: rare: 4 archived performances [3]\n- **Percent Wolf**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [3]\n- **I've Got the Sex**: back after 61 archived shows (974 days) [3]\n- **Days**: rare: 4 archived performances [3]\n- **Through This Fire**: rare: 3 archived performances [3]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **tMG2026-08-15** (recommended): matrix (soundboard mixed with audience mics); 23 songs; 99 min [1]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Stage talk about: No Children [1]\n- Outdoor show beside a pyramid; the real sunset fell directly behind the band while they played [1]\n- Unlike other shows, this one had no Days backdrop; the natural sunset took its place [1]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **tMG2026-08-15**: taped by Kyle Kennelly & Emerald Green; transferred by Kyle Kennelly; source: SBD > PCM A10 (24/48 WAV) + FR-AV2 > DPA 4060s (Healy Onstage 48/32 WAV) [1]. Also: Taped with DPA 4060 omni microphones and windscreens; Brandon Eggleston helped with the taping [1]",
